==Battleground==
*1 [[Golem Sunfish]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage debuts two enemies: Golem Sunfish and J.J. Jackrabbit. Golem Sunfish is a variant of Sunfish Jones where his first hit can Curse your units while his other two hits can Freeze, while J.J. Jackrabbit is a Red enemy with low endurance and high damage. In this level specifically, the Jackrabbits die extremely quickly to [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], while you can combo [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] to burst down Golem Sunfish. [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] works well as a tank for Elder Sloth, and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] works as a general damage dealer for both Elder Sloth and Golem Sunfish.

===3 Crown Strategy===
The Jackrabbits are not fun to fight. On 3 Crown, you can either choose to rush Golem Sunfish before things get too hectic, or just ride the storm out and brute force this level.

If you want to rush the level, use a Rich Cat, [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], Doron's second form, and high damage units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] to murder Golem Sunfish fast.

For a brute force strategy, your main goal is just killing the Jackrabbits fast. A high-levelled [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] does great, while [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] are rushers suitable for killing Jackrabbit, although Supercar's interaction is a trade that you might need to learn first. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]'s increased range also allows it to work. Supercar's Knockback ability allows you to push Elder Sloth back and have your damage dealers like Courier directly hit Golem Sunfish, while Awakened Doron's Colossus Slayer lets him deal extra damage to the Jackrabbits and push back Golem Sunfish if it's getting too close to your base.

